<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrew II of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1177–<a href="/years/1235">1235</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Andrew II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrew II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1205, of the Árpád dynasty. He led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-crusade">Fifth Crusade</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a> in 1217–1218 and spent heavily on wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, granting away royal estates to his supporters. Pressure from the lesser nobility forced him to issue the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1222">Golden Bull of 1222</a>, which limited royal power. He was the father of Béla IV and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-of-hungary">Saint Elizabeth of Hungary</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andrew-ii-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Andrew II of Hungary" width="320" height="339" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: György Klösz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andrew_II_seal_1224.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
